  "section": {
    "heading": "## User library \u2014 the log-in page says how to get an account",
    "text": "- The log-in page says how to get an account.",
    "smoke": [
      "- Signed out, open the log-in page: the line under Forgot password opens sign-up, or the invite request where sign-up is closed."
    ]
  },
  "notes": "Piece 1 of the sign-up plan, the library's part. Every page carries at load whether sign-up is open (user-server SignInPageFactsScript, the product's invite rule turned around; the key and type in @proteinjs/user); user-ui SignInPageFacts reads it at first paint. The log-in page gains one line under Forgot password (open: to /signup; closed: the product's registered line through user-ui AuthPageProduct, or none). The sign-up page without an invite renders at once from the fact (form or closed panel; no call, no gray bars); with an invite nothing changes. A signed-in person who opens either page is replaced to Home by the router. The app's half is the app branch of the same name, which registers the product's words and opens the setting on dev and test. Held: nothing published."
